Data licence — data-matched releases
====================================

The MIT licence in LICENSE covers the code in this repository. It does not
cover the data published in this repository's releases, and no licence is
granted over that data.

The matched-data files are an internal build artifact. They exist so
clusterflick.com can show a film's ratings next to its screenings, with each
score linked back to the source it came from — which is how the site meets the
attribution those sources ask for. They are published here because the pipeline
runs in the open, not as a dataset offered for reuse.

Every rating in them comes from somewhere else: IMDb, Letterboxd, Metacritic,
Rotten Tomatoes, The Movie Database and the Bechdel Test. Clusterflick holds no
rights in any of it and grants none. Two of those sources carry terms worth
naming outright:

  * Bechdel Test ratings are licensed under CC BY-NC 3.0
    (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/3.0/). Attribution is required
    wherever they are shown, and neither they nor anything built on them may be
    put to commercial use. Every matched entry carries a `url` back to the
    film's page on bechdeltest.com for that purpose.
  * IMDb material is used under IMDb's own non-commercial terms, which carry
    an attribution requirement of their own. Read them at
    https://developer.imdb.com/non-commercial-datasets/ rather than relying on
    a copy here.

Concretely:

  * No licence is granted over these releases. Clusterflick does not hold the
    rights it would need to grant one.
  * There are no schema guarantees. The shape, the field names and the file
